.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH sam-jail-verify 1 2026-11-10 "SAM 0.1.0" "SAM - Sandboxed AppImage Manager"
.SH NAME
sam\-jail\-verify \- Check that the app\*(Aqs sandbox gives it exactly what its settings say: starts the sandbox with a probe instead of the app. Also takes an AppImage without a sandbox: then the settings it would get are checked (nothing is unpacked or stored)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsam\-jail verify\fR [\fB\-\-permissions\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIAPP\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check that the app\*(Aqs sandbox gives it exactly what its settings say: starts the sandbox with a probe instead of the app. Also takes an AppImage without a sandbox: then the settings it would get are checked (nothing is unpacked or stored)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-permissions\-stdin\fR
Check these settings (a PermissionSet as JSON on stdin) for an AppImage without a sandbox, instead of SAM\*(Aqs recommendation
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIAPP\fR>

